// THE FIFTH, NOT THE OCTAVE.
// leaderofearth spans an octave (2:1) because authority wants somewhere to go.
// Jaimla spans a perfect fifth — F3 (174.61 Hz) to C4 (261.63 Hz), a ratio of
// 3:2, the most consonant interval there is. The narrowness IS the intimacy:
// a wide range reads as bright and excitable, a narrow low-lying one reads as
// close. Restraint is what makes a voice alluring; reach is what makes it loud.
//
// The geometric centre of that fifth is sqrt(174.61 x 261.63) = 213.8 Hz, which
// lands within 2% of 210 — the f0 that NeuralVoiceEngine.js already assigns to
// the jaimla profile (src/NeuralVoiceEngine.js:50-55, sid 4, female). This voice
// is tuned to the Jaimla mindX already had, not to a new invention.
pitch 175 262

// A shorter vocal tract: F1-F3 lifted in frequency and widened, which is what
// reads as feminine. But the upper formants are kept SOFT in amplitude rather
// than bright — brightness is where a female formant set turns shrill, and
// enchantment is the opposite of piercing.
formant 0 100 130 118
formant 1 116 128 112
formant 2 122 124 104
formant 3 118 116  92
formant 4 112 108  78
formant 5 106 100  62
formant 6  98  90  42
formant 7  92  84  30
formant 8  88  80  24

// Air over edge. The mid carries her; the treble is present enough to sparkle
// and deliberately short of sibilance.
tone 400 205 1100 235 2400 130

// BREATH IS THE VOICE.
// Softness here is not lower volume, it is breath in the tone — an unpressed
// fold with air moving past it. breath opens the whole register and breathw
// widens the noise band so it reads as warmth rather than as hiss.
breath  2 4 5 5 5 5 4 3
breathw 100 150 165 165 165 165 150 120
voicing 62
consonants 58 46
roughness 0
flutter 2

// A soft halo, slightly longer and quieter than leaderofearth's hall — near,
// not grand.
echo 110 9

// ENCHANTING MEANS MOVING.
// leaderofearth flattens its contour to land conclusions; Jaimla does the
// opposite and keeps the full default melody, because the pleasure of this
// voice is that it rises and falls. Stress is carried by PITCH (stressAdd)
// rather than by loudness (stressAmp held low and nearly flat) — emphasis
// that leans in instead of pushing.
intonation 1
stressAmp   14 14 15 15 16 16 17 17
stressAdd    0 10 25 40 55 70 100 120
